True-cliff rock oolong of the heritage Aijiao Wulong ("dwarf-legged wulong") cultivar from the Zhuke grove — Shiqi "17" sells it as "Dwarf-Legged Wulong".

As a producer who likes to age his yancha, this is 17''s favorite varietal to work with due to its ability to maintain its distinctive aroma-flavor characteristics in storage longer than others. A heritage cultivar with a history of over 100 years representing some of the earliest genetic lines of breeding in the Beiyuan tribute tea area, this cultivar likely was named after its smaller leaf, densely branched, lower to the ground, scrubbier growth pattern.', 'Zhuke, Wuyishan, Nanping, Fujian, China', 'oolong', 'true_tea', 'medium', 95, 1, 6, 'Use 5g per 150ml at 95–100°C. Quick rinse; steep 20–40 seconds; re-steep 5–7 times.', ARRAY['Mineral', 'Floral', 'Roasted', 'Distinctive']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '#D4852A', 48, 55, 60, 30, 'default', 'Teapp', NULL, TRUE),
