  ('Hui Yuan Keng Beidou Da Hong Pao', 'hui-yuan-keng-beidou-da-hong-pao', 'Huìyuàn Kēng Běidǒu Dàhóngpáo', '慧苑坑北斗大红袍', 'The core tea production arena in the Wuyi Mountains referred to as 正岩 zheng yan "true cliff" is regarded as the highest pedigree of terroir when it comes to Rock Oolong: jagged, idyllic cliffs harbor tea gardens between them, feeding the soil a consistent runoff of minerals experienced in the finished tea as 岩韵 yan yun "rock charm". All ten teas rested 1–2 years after their last roasting, allowing the necessary 退火 "retreating fire".

