High-fire Da Hong Pao of the true Beidou ("Big Dipper") DHP cultivar from Hui Yuan Keng — the darkest, richest, most layered of the series, with a bit of ripened age.

The darkest, most roastiest yancha (with a nice ripened bit of age on it as well), this high fire Da Hong Pao is arguably the most rich and layered of the bunch. Pure Mrs. Trunchbull''s cake. Also featured in the FIRE SET box.', 'Hui Yuan Keng, Wuyishan, Nanping, Fujian, China', 'oolong', 'true_tea', 'medium', 95, 1, 6, 'Use 5g per 150ml at 95–100°C. Quick rinse; steep 20–40 seconds; re-steep 5–7 times.', ARRAY['Roasted', 'Rich', 'Layered', 'Mineral']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '#D4852A', 55, 75, 72, 28, 'default', 'Teapp', NULL, TRUE);
